{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Enable a persistent host firewall on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The nftables ruleset was installed, enabled, and active before restart. A confirmed reboot changed the boot identity, after which nftables was active and enabled with the same configuration checksum and restored live ruleset.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8fee84fd94264419","cmd-6bf3a11927b94707","cmd-676f16e1b1194343","cmd-22e170c0b8bd4f54","cmd-73a276a4c6de4796","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Permit inbound SSH (TCP/22) and TCP/8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After reboot, simultaneous listeners on TCP/22, TCP/8080, and TCP/8081 were established. Connections through node1's managed IP reached the listeners on ports 22 and 8080 and received port-specific application responses.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0bc03cd223f4470d","cmd-6a804b60b5314238"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Reject unrelated inbound connections.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The recovered live input chain ends in an active reject rule. A post-reboot connection to the confirmed listening TCP/8081 service through node1's managed IP was immediately refused while ports 22 and 8080 succeeded, directly demonstrating rejection rather than absence of a listener.","evidence_ids":["cmd-73a276a4c6de4796","cmd-0bc03cd223f4470d","cmd-6a804b60b5314238"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The persistent configuration and service enablement were required (`cmd-8fee84fd94264419`); the temporary listeners, namespaces, and veth interfaces supported bounded pre- and post-restart functional tests (`cmd-4d7e0b6767c3441c`, `cmd-0bc03cd223f4470d`) and were fully removed (`cmd-0b3679089f5c4705`, `cmd-298d4992c5424665`). The reboot served both persistence validation and the mandatory restart protocol (`cmd-676f16e1b1194343`). Final snapshots show healthy package state, no test listeners or residue, and only the pre-existing failed SSH service. The restart protocol is complete and consistent with the fixed boot-identity observations.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8fee84fd94264419","cmd-4d7e0b6767c3441c","cmd-0b3679089f5c4705","cmd-676f16e1b1194343","cmd-0bc03cd223f4470d","cmd-298d4992c5424665","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Node1 has an enabled nftables firewall that survived a verified reboot, permits TCP/22 and TCP/8080, and actively rejects unrelated inbound TCP traffic. The provider-wide restart evidence for the sole managed node includes a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered network and firewall state, unchanged persistent configuration, and post-restart behavioral validation.","limitations":["Functional testing used temporary listeners because no SSH or TCP/8080 application service was present; this directly verifies firewall admission but not production application health, which was not required.","The negative behavioral test sampled TCP/8081; broader rejection is supported by the observed catch-all input-chain reject rule rather than exhaustive tests of every unrelated port and protocol."]}
